---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/ai-progress-notes/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="ed-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">Mental health EHR</a>{" "}
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">
          AI Progress Notes for Therapists: SOAP &amp; DAP
        </span>
      </nav>
      <section class="ed-hero">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">AI progress notes for mental health</div>
          <h1>
            Start with the conversation.
            <br />
            <em>Finish with your note.</em>
          </h1>
          <p class="ed-dek">
            Otto turns session audio into a SOAP or DAP draft. Review the
            details, make it your own, and sign a note that reflects the care
            you provided.
          </p>
          <div class="ed-actions">
            <a class="button" href="/waitlist/">
              Join the waitlist ↗
            </a>
            <a class="text-link" href="/demo/#watch">
              Watch the 2-minute demo ↗
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="micro">
            For independent mental health practices · Built by Tebra
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-hero-art">
          <div class="art">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 640 500"
              preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <rect width="640" height="500" fill="#dce7de" />
              <circle cx="490" cy="80" r="200" fill="#c5d7ce" />
              <g transform="translate(165 55) rotate(-7 145 180)">
                <rect
                  x="14"
                  y="16"
                  width="290"
                  height="350"
                  rx="14"
                  fill="#004852"
                  opacity=".1"
                />
                <rect width="290" height="350" rx="14" fill="#fffdf8" />
                <path
                  d="M28 42h95"
                  stroke="#004852"
                  stroke-width="6"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                />
                <g fill="#004852">
                  <rect x="28" y="80" width="34" height="34" rx="10" />
                  <rect x="28" y="143" width="34" height="34" rx="10" />
                  <rect x="28" y="206" width="34" height="34" rx="10" />
                  <rect x="28" y="269" width="34" height="34" rx="10" />
                </g>
                <g stroke="#a6bfb2" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round">
                  <path d="M80 91h170m-170 15h130M80 154h170m-170 15h110M80 217h170m-170 15h145M80 280h170m-170 15h120" />
                </g>
                <g
                  fill="#f6f3eb"
                  font-family="sans-serif"
                  font-size="17"
                  text-anchor="middle"
                >
                  <text x="45" y="103">
                    S
                  </text>
                  <text x="45" y="166">
                    O
                  </text>
                  <text x="45" y="229">
                    A
                  </text>
                  <text x="45" y="292">
                    P
                  </text>
                </g>
              </g>
              <circle cx="480" cy="365" r="48" fill="#b85c38" />
              <path
                d="m460 365 15 15 27-32"
                fill="none"
                stroke="#fffdf8"
                stroke-width="4"
                stroke-linecap="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Documentation that carries forward</span>
            <h2>There is useful work after the draft.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Once you sign, Otto proposes structured chart updates from the final
            note. You decide what belongs in the record before the next visit.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>Capture with consent</h3>
            <p>
              Use the appropriate patient-consent process before recording. Otto
              uses session audio to prepare the draft.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>Review and sign</h3>
            <p>
              Check the account of the visit, clinical interpretation, and plan.
              Edit the note before adding your signature.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Confirm the chart changes</h3>
            <p>
              Review proposed diagnoses, treatment-plan items, and medication
              updates. Accept or dismiss each item.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-story">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Two familiar formats</span>
          <h2>
            SOAP or DAP.
            <br />
            Your way of documenting.
          </h2>
          <p>
            Use the structure that fits your practice. SOAP separates subjective
            reports, observations, assessment, and plan. DAP brings the visit
            information together under data, assessment, and plan.
          </p>
          <p>
            Explore our examples and editable templates to see the difference
            before trying Otto’s documentation workflow.
          </p>
          <div class="ed-resources">
            <a href="/templates/soap-notes/">SOAP template ↗</a>
            <a href="/templates/dap-notes/">DAP template ↗</a>
            <a href="/blog/soap-vs-dap-notes/">Compare formats ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-visual">
          <div class="ed-note">
            <div class="ed-note-top">
              <img
                src="/assets/otto-logo.svg"
                alt="Otto"
                width="58"
                height="30"
              />
              <span>Draft for review</span>
            </div>
            <h3>The conversation, organized.</h3>
            <p class="micro">Fictional example · SOAP structure</p>
            <div class="ed-note-row">
              <b>S</b>
              <div>
                <strong>Subjective</strong>
                <p>
                  Client described difficulty setting boundaries around work
                  messages.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ed-note-row">
              <b>O</b>
              <div>
                <strong>Objective</strong>
                <p>
                  Client practiced a response to an after-hours request during
                  the session.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ed-note-row">
              <b>A</b>
              <div>
                <strong>Assessment</strong>
                <p>
                  Add your clinical assessment after reviewing the encounter.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ed-note-row">
              <b>P</b>
              <div>
                <strong>Plan</strong>
                <p>
                  Revisit the boundary-setting practice at the next appointment.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ed-approval">
            <p>You review, edit, and sign the final note.</p>
            <span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Illustrative excerpt, not a clinical record or product screenshot.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Your record, your review</span>
            <h2>Keep the clinical decisions visible.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            A useful draft needs a clear path for correction. Otto’s note
            workflow includes an editor, signature, and addenda, with separate
            confirmation for structured chart updates.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>See the draft’s origin</h3>
            <p>
              An AI provenance badge identifies the draft. Read the entire note
              and correct anything the encounter does not support.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>Preserve your judgment</h3>
            <p>
              You decide what the note says and when it is ready to sign.
              Suggested clinical changes require your confirmation.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Carry context into next time</h3>
            <p>
              The patient summary and last-session highlights connect
              documentation with preparation for the next encounter.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-faq">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</span>
          <h2>Get to know the details.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Can I edit the AI-generated note?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. Otto provides a draft for your review. You can edit it before
              signing and use the available addendum workflow for later
              corrections.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Does Otto support custom note templates?</summary>
            <p>
              The formats described in this preview are SOAP and DAP. Confirm
              any need for reusable custom templates, specialty-specific forms,
              or other formats with the team.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What happens after I sign?</summary>
            <p>
              Otto proposes structured updates from the signed note. Review and
              confirm the items you want in the patient record, then continue
              through the payment workflow.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How are recording and patient data handled?</summary>
            <p>
              Review the <a href="/security/">security and data questions</a>{" "}
              with the Otto team, including the applicable BAA, recording
              consent, retention, and AI processing terms.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-close">
        <div>
          <h2>See what a connected practice day can feel like.</h2>
          <p>
            Watch Otto carry a visit from preparation through documentation and
            payment. Then tell us about the way you practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
          Join the waitlist ↗
        </a>
      </section>
      <p class="ed-source">
        Product details checked against{" "}
        <a href="https://otto.tebra.com/">Otto’s public website</a> on October
        16, 2026. Confirm availability and service terms for your practice.
        Workflow examples are illustrative and use fictional information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
